.TH OB_TCP_SERVER 1 "September 2026" "orderbook-dbengine 0.1.0" "Orderbook DB Engine"
.SH NAME
ob_tcp_server \- Level 2 orderbook database server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ob_tcp_server
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ob_tcp_server
.B \-\-config
.I path
.RB [ \-\-print\-config ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ob_tcp_server
serves Level 2 orderbook data over a line-oriented TCP protocol. It stores writes in a
write-ahead log, keeps live depth in structure-of-arrays buffers, and flushes to columnar
segments with delta, zigzag and Simple8b compression.
.PP
The server runs natively on the host. There is no containerised deployment path and there will
not be one: a container layer between the engine and the hardware defeats the point of an engine
tuned for specific hardware.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Every option is both a command-line flag and a key in the configuration file, because the file is
rewritten into arguments and handed to the same parser. A key is a flag name without the leading
dashes.
.PP
A flag overrides the file; the file overrides the default. Precedence needs no merge rule: the
file's arguments simply come first.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Read settings from
.IR path .
A missing file, an unknown key, a line without an
.BR = ,
a duplicated key or a value of the wrong type stops the start rather than being ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the resolved configuration with the provenance of each value \(em default, file or command
line \(em and exit without opening a port. A list of values does not say which of them you chose,
and not opening a port matters because a taken port is one of the situations you reach for this in.
.SH OPTIONS
Only the ones an operator changes first. The full set is in
.B \-\-print\-config
output and in
.IR /usr/share/doc/orderbook\-dbengine/cli.md .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
TCP port for clients. Default 9090.
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " path"
Where the write-ahead log and columnar segments live. Default
.IR /tmp/ob_data ,
and the package ships
.I /var/lib/orderbook
in its configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-sessions " n"
Client connections accepted at once. Default 64. Each costs a file descriptor; see
.B LimitNOFILE
in the shipped unit.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
.BR ERROR ,
.BR WARN ,
.B INFO
or
.BR DEBUG .
Default INFO, in both the shipped configuration and the binary. This line said DEBUG in the
binary, which was wrong: the default is
.B INFO
in
.IR TcpServerConfig ,
and the mistaken sentence is what made a log-volume estimate wrong by an order of magnitude while
chasing a hung node.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-port " n"
Prometheus endpoint. 0 disables it.
.TP
.BI \-\-coordinator\-endpoints " urls"
Comma-separated etcd endpoints. Required for automatic failover and for multi-master.
.TP
.B \-\-multi\-master
Every node accepts writes; conflicts resolve by hybrid logical clock and last-writer-wins.
Requires
.B \-\-coordinator\-endpoints
and
.BR \-\-mm\-node\-id ,
and is refused together with
.B \-\-read\-only
or with single-primary replication rather than one of them being silently preferred.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/orderbook/ob.conf
Shipped configuration. Marked as a configuration file, so a package upgrade does not overwrite
local changes.
.TP
.I /var/lib/orderbook
Default state directory in the shipped configuration. Created by systemd through
.BR StateDirectory= ,
so the package does not have to create it and then hope nothing changes its ownership.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/ob_tcp_server.service
Shipped unit.
.SH SECURITY
.B The wire protocol authenticates and does not encrypt.
Client sessions authenticate with
.B \-\-auth\-secret\-file
and the replication and multi\-master links with
.BR \-\-cluster\-secret\-file ,
by challenge\-response over HMAC\-SHA256, so a secret never crosses the wire. Both are off by
default and the startup log warns for each disabled surface. Nothing is encrypted, so every query
and every row is readable by anything on the path: do not expose a node outside a trusted network.
The two secret files must not contain the same secret \- a client holding the cluster secret can
present itself as a replica \- and the start is refused if they do. See
.IR SECURITY.md .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown, or
.B \-\-print\-config
completing.
.TP
.B 1
A command line or configuration file the server does not fully understand, a port it cannot bind,
or a data directory it cannot open. The server refuses to start rather than starting with a
configuration nobody intended.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR etcd (1)
